{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושפך את דמו וכסהו בעפר", :translit "v'shafach et damo v'chisahu b'afar", :gloss "and he shall pour out its blood and cover it with dust"} {:he "דם חיה ועוף", :translit "dam chayah v'of", :gloss "blood of a wild animal and of a bird"} {:he "טעונין כסוי", :translit "t'chonin kisuy", :gloss "require covering"} {:he "שאין מקריבין ממנו על המזבח", :translit "she'ein mak'rin mimenu al ha-mizbe'ach", :gloss "for they are not offered from it upon the altar"} {:he "שלא תהא מדת הדין מקטרגת", :translit "sh'lo t'hei midat ha-din m'kat'rigeret", :gloss "lest the attribute of judgment prosecute"} {:he "איך דם יאכל דם", :translit "eich dam yo'chel dam", :gloss "how does blood consume blood"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The phrase 'איך דם יאכל דם' echoes Obadiah 1:6 as a prooftext for why unconsecrated blood must be hidden."}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah teaches that the blood of a wild animal (חיה) and of a bird (עוף) requires covering, whereas the blood of a domesticated animal (בהמה) does not, since only domesticated animals are offered on the altar (Keritot 28b). The phrase 'how is it that blood consumes blood' alludes to Obadiah 1:6, 'איך נחתך איך יאכל דם'.", :sources ["Keritot 28b" "Obadiah 1:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The phrase 'איך דם יאכל דם' echoes Obadiah 1:6 as a prooftext for why unconsecrated blood must be hidden.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:54.145791503Z", :model "glm-5.2"}